{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects","id":1305131,"title":"Spheres for computation efffects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-15T13:58:12-07:00","id":1305131,"title":"Spheres for computation efffects","content":"Computation is a part of all Sphere Magick, but I don't see any clear way to use Spheres for a direct computation, and that feels... wrong. <br /> <br /> After all, it is certainly possible to create a computer that can make the computation with Matter, or to even use a Mind effect that allows someone to do more complex math in their head. It's also possible with Entropy to &quot;randomly&quot; hit keys and get the first thousand digits of pi. <br /> <br /> What about solving the n-body problem for like 1000 objects? What about proving the Riemann Hypothesis? Proving that P\u2260NP? Calculating tip for a party of 16?<br /> <br /> It certainly seems like it would be in the hypothetical Information Sphere that the VAs are so keep about, but how would that even work? Given Information theory, and how it is tied to entropy, would the Entropy Sphere be the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25164-ustice","name":"Ustice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T23:44:33-07:00","id":1305212,"title":"","content":"It might be unintuitive about how to handle calculations with Magick (aside of, yes, boosting your mind with the Mind sphere and such), but the actual solution is hinted at by a certain Technocratic Sphere that the VAs can also learn: <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Data Sphere.<br /> <br /> I.e. 'Correspondence'.<br /> It makes sense, too - if you consider how calculations happen, you can see it as making a connection (Correspondence/Data) from the original Problem to the Solution, through a series of changes (Entropy).<br /> <br /> So it's either simply just the Data/Correspondence Sphere (To essentially establish a connection between the Problem Data and the Solution and thus 'finding' the Solution without any steps in between - which might be a flavor of mysterious Quantum computing), or possibly Data/Correspondence + Entropy to get all the mathematical steps in between the Problem Data and the Solution.<br /> <br /> If you combine Data or Data/Entropy with the Mind sphere, you could 'automatically' do calculations in your head instead of just relying on enhanced stats or the 'Lightning Calculator' through the Mind Sphere alone, and if you combine it with Forces you could aplly it to an electronic computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-16-2019, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T05:39:54-07:00","id":1305245,"title":"","content":"I always took Mind as being more than the Sphere you can use to control and enhance minds but also the Sphere that manipulates abstract concepts and other constructs of the mind.<br /> <br /> I think that because in most old books (before Data was a thing) Mind was used for things like traducing or deciphering a text...and that can't be done by enhancing your brain (you need knowledge more than capacity) nor by &quot;mind reading&quot; (most books haven't minds to read). I took that as Mind being able to affect abstract things like language and meaning.<br /> <br /> Maths ARE just a language, a formal one, and logic it's a property of the mind. Hence I would argue that other than Data/Entropy, Mind should be able to manipulate calculations and computation problems <i>directly</i> (rather than just making you good at it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-16-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T05:43:03-07:00","id":1305246,"title":"","content":"A fair argument!<br /> While it wouldn't apply to computers, I can see the Mind sphere being able to automate some things in the mind of a person - the type of things you don't really need to think about anymore when you've practiced them. Language is excellent for that, as are certain degrees of math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T09:39:41-07:00","id":1305282,"title":"","content":"Mind + various Spheres would be how you calculate something, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> For example, a Mage could use Mind, Time, Correspondence and Forces to determine something important with regards to the space-time continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T11:43:36-07:00","id":1305307,"title":"","content":"Conceptual effects get tricky precisely because they are conceptual. Even in the real world there is a strong line of thought that Mathematics is not real and exists entirely within the human mind. When you take this into Mage you start getting really strange questions. For instance, if an Etherite or a Hermetic invents a whole new type of mathematics, can you target that? Does it matter if you do?<br /> <br /> The two Spheres with the strongest claim on conceptual matters are Mind and Spirit. Mind because concepts exist within and are products of the mind. Spirit because the High Umbra is the realm of the conceptual.<br /> <br /> The answers would probably get even stranger if you wanted to alter mathematics, such as creating a zone where pi = 3.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T15:11:10-07:00","id":1305343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1305307#post1305307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptual effects get tricky precisely because they are conceptual. Even in the real world there is a strong line of thought that Mathematics is not real and exists entirely within the human mind. When you take this into Mage you start getting really strange questions. For instance, if an Etherite or a Hermetic invents a whole new type of mathematics, can you target that? Does it matter if you do?<br /> <br /> The two Spheres with the strongest claim on conceptual matters are Mind and Spirit. Mind because concepts exist within and are products of the mind. Spirit because the High Umbra is the realm of the conceptual.<br /> <br /> The answers would probably get even stranger if you wanted to alter mathematics, such as creating a zone where pi = 3.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Terry Pratchett book did have a machine that turns pi into 3. Essentially its designer was completely furious with &quot;God&quot; or whoever created the world for making it such an irrational and pointlessly long number... and he wanted to fix it.<br /> <br /> Basically anything you put into the machine gets... warped, and I believe I remember it has some horribly damaging effect with regards to the rest of the world. This would be in either Making Money or Going Postal, not certain which.<br /> <br /> And yeah if you were to create your own Realm, I suppose that a mixture of Mind (concepts), Correspondence (shapes and lengths), Entropy (breaking down the concept of pi and giving this new concept a sort of stasis so that it isn't broken down) and Spirit (realm shenanigans, plus higher concepts that have spiritual aspects) could allow you to redefine Pi as 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T21:58:09-07:00","id":1305400,"title":"","content":"Another thing would be that the paradigm absolutely matters. Techocracts and Technomancers, yes. Hermetics... Maybe. Others? No, just no.<br /> <br /> Also, this is just a fascinating idea to me. I think ultimately it falls under &quot;magic enhancing abilities&quot; and give a -3 difficulty. That said... It's still a neat conceptual question:<br /> <br /> High school aged PC: &quot;I want to use magic to do my homework.&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Uh...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":".  More stuff. 04-17-2019, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:18:32-07:00","id":1305463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1305400#post1305400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermetics... Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hermetics are direct inheritors of the pythagorean Mathematics, and also have Plato (<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;Let no one ignorant of geometry enter&quot; </span></span>) as their inspiration. They're totally going to have matemagicians.<br /> <br /> I imagine they would err towards Mind/Spirit and High Umbra shenanigans rather than Data/Entropy, as their classic approach meshes well with concepts existing &quot;out there&quot; (in the world of forms or the mind of God).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Others? No, just no. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be so sure. Paradigm absolutely matters but many old mystical cultures were fond of mathematics. I wouldn't discount some Choristers having Sacred Geometry and doing matemagicks to approach pi in order to build better temples or ancient Mayan astrologists/astronomists under the Verbena.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to ponder if these would count, at least partially, as &quot;technomancers&quot; (Scientific Mystics)...but if they do Hermetics should be on that camp too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, this is just a fascinating idea to me. I think ultimately it falls under &quot;magic enhancing abilities&quot; and give a -3 difficulty. That said... It's still a neat conceptual question:<br /> <br /> High school aged PC: &quot;I want to use magic to do my homework.&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Uh...&quot; </div> </div> </div>Technomancers know well how booring and time consuming can be to solve calculations by yourself, and that's why they've used their magick to create a device that helps one to manipulate these abstract concepts, aptly called &quot;the calculator&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's notheworthy that matemagicians probably use maths as Instrument, and thus need to have that Science leveled up to the maximum Sphere needed to cast the spell. So to use mathemagics to solve a problem our lazy student would <i>probably </i>need to be able to solve it by mundane means. Heck, I think she would need to be way beyond High School level to do that. Magick would fasten and perfect the process, however, and thus allow to do calculations that are too long and tedious to solve or involve too much data.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly what Computers do for Computation...Magick!<br /> <br /> The idea here it's to affect concepts directly. To be able to &quot;summon&quot; the answer as long as you have a general idea about where to find it. I think that converting that to a -3 it's kinda booring and not the only option. One should use the rules that are better to model the narrative of the spell. Summoning the homework of a good student and copying it with Matter, for instance, wouldn't fall under &quot;magic enhancing abilities&quot; rules but under conjuration and transmutation rules.<br /> <br /> The rules mentioned in the spellcasting section don't cover everything that should be used to model a spell and the ST is encouraged to get creative at that point. RAW you can always go the the general table of &quot;Magickal Feats&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-17-2019, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T13:03:20-07:00","id":1305537,"title":"","content":"The power of math is seeming depth that can come out of simple rules, and, to quote Eugene Wigner, there's the question of &quot;The Unreasonable Effectiveness of Mathematics in the Natural Sciences&quot;. We don't have much example to say that magic can do computation in abstract systems. For instance, I don't think it'd be reasonable to have a spell that could complete a book for an author that were not using Time to bring forward the work, Mind to compel the writing, or in some way creating something to finish the work that weren't either a proxy for the author or a substitute, either way, it's not suddenly generating the ending.<br /> <br /> Math to me is similar. Magic can not itself force actions from an abstract system but interface with things using it. When magic seems to be acting on abstract systems it's more acting on the embodiments of that system. Magic can speed up computation, but does not allow for sudden realization of answers except in forcing rules changes to allow for them. The 1,000 body problem may have no natural closed form solution but with enough successes you could create a system with a closed form solution because forces were shoving it into that configuration but that doesn't make the solution real in the general case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:51:41-07:00","id":1308761,"title":"","content":"I think that this question is harder from a Mathematical Realist perspective, where math isn't a product of the mind, but actual objective &quot;things&quot; within the universe.<br /> <br /> The more that I think about it, Entropy is the sphere that handles calculations and logic. It's what is needed to have conditional effects, which implies that it works with if-then logic.<br /> <br /> Prime factorization is pretty trivial with Entropy, isn't it? Pick any integer that has two prime factors that you want. Then set up your computer to pick two random integers less than the original, and with Entropy adjust the outcome to so that their product is the original number, and then just recursively apply that. BOOM P=NP. Bye-bye, public key encryption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25164-ustice","name":"Ustice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T08:19:33-07:00","id":1308928,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that Correspondence covers computation far better than Entropy does. In fact, I see it as the go-to Sphere for math-oriented magick. To me, Entropy is more focused on probability and statistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:22:44-07:00","id":1308954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1308928#post1308928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to think that Correspondence covers computation far better than Entropy does. In fact, I see it as the go-to Sphere for math-oriented magick. To me, Entropy is more focused on probability and statistics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting way of looking at it. Is that because math is frequently about relationships and Correspondence is the sphere or relationships?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T14:05:28-07:00","id":1309007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1308954#post1308954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting way of looking at it. Is that because math is frequently about relationships and Correspondence is the sphere or relationships?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty much why I used Correspondence in my own post. Correspondence to make a simple connection from the formula to the result, or Correspondence AND Entropy, to actually get the in-betweens from the original formula to the result with the sphere of change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T21:48:04-07:00","id":1309098,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this all comes down to paradigm. Since this is one of those gray areas, as a Storyteller, I would just go with whichever worked with the character\u2019s paradigm. <br /> <br /> Probability and statistics _are_ math. Baye\u2019s Theorem is at the heart of any of it.<br /> <br /> Correspondence is about tracing entanglements, and I can see (especially when we look at it through the lens of the Data interpretation). <br /> <br /> I appreciate your comments and insights. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25164-ustice","name":"Ustice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T22:02:17-07:00","id":1309104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1305537#post1305537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Math to me is similar. Magic can not itself force actions from an abstract system but interface with things using it. When magic seems to be acting on abstract systems it's more acting on the embodiments of that system. Magic can speed up computation, but does not allow for sudden realization of answers except in forcing rules changes to allow for them. The 1,000 body problem may have no natural closed form solution but with enough successes you could create a system with a closed form solution because forces were shoving it into that configuration but that doesn't make the solution real in the general case.</div> </div> </div> </div>For most mages, I would agree here, but I think that the Virtual Adepts in particular highlight the case where this is no longer consistent. If I understand the source code of the Universe, then I can use that to graph a function, like a sphere. I can make a simple adder and itterators. If I have access to logic tools, then I can do math. The question would be whether this can be run on the substrate of the Universe, but if I light some LEDs in a particular pattern based on the mathmatical calculations and logical flow, then there is simply no functional difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25164-ustice","name":"Ustice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T12:11:50-07:00","id":1309249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1308954#post1308954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting way of looking at it. Is that because math is frequently about relationships and Correspondence is the sphere or relationships?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of it. Another part of it is the connection between Correspondence, Geometry, and Trigonometry: that's where the spatial aspects of Correspondence factor in. <br /> <br /> Also, Correspondence is intimately connected to the Digital Web, which is the realm of computation made manifest. Then there's the Technocratic variant of Correspondence, namely Data: for the record, I had been using Correspondence in that fashion for decades before the Revised NWO Convention Book formalized the notion that Correspondence is about Data. If anything, the NWO's Data Sphere fails to grasp the full extent of what Correspondence is, just as the Void Engineers focus on the geometric aspects with their Void Correspondence (briefly mentioned in the Revised VE Convention Book) and tend to overlook the Data aspects. Even asking the Traditions, most tend to focus on the Sympathetic Links and assume that that's what the Sphere is all about. <br /> <br /> Only the Virtual Adepts truly grasp the full scope of the Sphere. There's a synergy between space, data, and Sympathy that produces something more expansive than just the sum of the parts \u2014 something that's hard to describe, but is internally mathematical in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T07:46:08-07:00","id":1309640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ustice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1309104#post1309104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For most mages, I would agree here, but I think that the Virtual Adepts in particular highlight the case where this is no longer consistent. If I understand the source code of the Universe, then I can use that to graph a function, like a sphere. I can make a simple adder and itterators. If I have access to logic tools, then I can do math. The question would be whether this can be run on the substrate of the Universe, but if I light some LEDs in a particular pattern based on the mathmatical calculations and logical flow, then there is simply no functional difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the problem here is conflating our notion of true with a paradigm's notion of true. For instance, to VA, they feel that correspondence should be able to cut an apple in half, but regardless of willpower, they still need matter/life to bisection something. There's also a gap between understanding the model and being able to manipulate it. Seeing the source code and editing it are different and the notion of editability is also a paradigm question. One could &quot;see&quot; the wave function for a phenomenon in physics but changing it directly at the source level rather than interacting directly with the system would fall outside that realm to me.<br /> <br /> The VAs think they're right but reality is under no obligation to comply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T08:20:49-07:00","id":1309653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1309640#post1309640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The VAs think they're right but reality is under no obligation to comply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it IS under obligation to comply if their player has bought the right Spheres :P<br /> <br /> I think reasonable to demand that to understand the maths underlying any particular phenomena you have to know the Sphere that senses/manipulates that phenomena. If you want to magicaly calculate the mass of Jupiter, you would need Matter 1 on top of whatever &quot;calculus Spheres&quot; you've learned because mass it's a property of the planet. To calculate the probability of an asteroid hitting the earth you would need Correspondence because it's a spatial relationship between discrete objects and Entropy because it's chance, but probably not Matter nor Forces unless you want to know extra stuff like the force of the impact or the durability of the object.<br /> <br /> The <i>real </i>problem comes when you want to calculate purely theoretical problems that have no relationship with easily targetable phenomena. Like non-euclidian stuff. There Spheres have left us mostly empty handed, barring, perhaps, Digital Web program manipulation trough Forces and/or Correspondence and some rare Rotes like Entropy decription and Mind language understanding.<br /> <br /> Rather than saying that these things are &quot;outside of magick reach&quot; in spite of the fact that you can actually find corporeal representations of them in the Umbra, I would rather suggest that perhaps these things are among the bajillon things magick can do yet wasn't ruled because, as stated in the Core (and in most RPG), rules can't cover ALL what a character can do in a roleplaying game, much less when you add a dimension so vast and unpredictable as the Spheres are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T09:59:30-07:00","id":1309669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1309653#post1309653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real problem comes when you want to calculate purely theoretical problems that have no relationship with easily targetable phenomena. Like non-euclidian stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> With all due respect, non-euclidean stuff is Correspondence \u2014 not <i>just</i> because Correspondence is the Sphere of pure mathematics<sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u2605</span></sup>, but also because \u201cnon-Euclidean\u201d is about geometry; and even if you don't buy that Correspondence is about pure math, it should be obvious that geometry is in its purview. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">\u2605 <i>Applied</i> math is a different story; that's where other Spheres come in.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:18:36-07:00","id":1309674,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're right about that. It is spatial relationships, even if they are weird relationships.<br /> <br /> More proof: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shade_Realm_of_Correspondence\" target=\"_blank\">The Shade Realm of Correspondence</a> it's described as having bizarre geometry. And what Sphere X can create/manipulate, Sphere X can sense/understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T17:33:47-07:00","id":1309956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects?p=1309653#post1309653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it IS under obligation to comply if their player has bought the right Spheres :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon, to clarify, in some paradigms, a given sphere has a winder domain than it does in other paradigms a la the &quot;VAs think that Correspondence by itself is enough to cut an apple&quot; but I don't think most STs would allow that. BUT! Your &quot;:P&quot; is noted. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T18:19:33-07:00","id":1309964,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I don't see the VAs believing that all you need is Correspondence. I <i>could</i> see a Correspondence-based variant of the \u201cA Bit of Spirit\u201d optional rule find in HDYDT: add a two-dot Correspondence requirement to whatever Sphere requirements the Effect would normally have. That said, there's a reason that's an optional rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}